  "body": "From the review of PR #165 (#156): https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/165#issuecomment-6713958418.\n\nThe workspace `serde_json` dependency lacks the `float_roundtrip` feature, so an off-round float written as `-14.966666666666667` reads back as `-14.966666666666669`. Stamps hash those values, so after save and load a stock-placed contour (and, since #156, every part or selection op once a stock was edited) reads Stale. It fails safe, since the post refuses until a regenerate, but it happens on every load. The same misread likely hits mesh coordinates too, staling imported models or losing picked faces.\n\nDone means: `serde_json = { version = \"1\", features = [\"float_roundtrip\"] }` in the workspace Cargo.toml. Pin: a project with an off-round stock placement and a generated contour saves, loads, and the contour reads Ok with every float bit-identical. Also check mesh vertex round-trip.",
